# WOLF — Market Data & Live Feeds

## Reuse existing stack

- Extend `server/marketData`, `MarketDataProvider`, `instrumentUniverse`, INDstocks client — do not add parallel brokers/feeds.
- Universes come only from the existing Universe / instrument-master system.

## Tokens & auth

- Access tokens stay server-side; never put them in `localStorage`, query strings, or frontend logs.
- Reuse existing connect/status/reconnect flows; sensible backoff, no infinite reconnect spam.

## Pipeline

```text
INDstocks → authenticated feed → MarketDataService → normalized events
  → shared state → analytics → strategy/radar → UI updates
```

- Prefer WebSocket/SSE for live; REST for config/history/CRUD.
- Backend owns candle construction for core calc timeframes (1m–1D as project supports).
- Multi-timeframe strategies request only needed TFs.

## Quality

- Isolate per-symbol errors so one failure cannot stop the scan engine.
- Do not persist every tick; persist configs/strategies/audit only as needed.
- Never show LIVE when the underlying connection is down; flag stale data.
